        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(security): add estimate-before-decode guard to base64 paths",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nLarge base64-encoded images can cause transient memory pressure during decoding. This PR adds a size estimation check before decoding base64 image data in CLI staging, provider image-parsing paths, and the Codex/OpenAI OAuth image-generation result route, and propagates the existing configured media size limit through these new guards.\n\n**Security impact**: Defense-in-depth against transient memory exhaustion from oversized base64 payloads.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Reuses the existing public `estimateBase64DecodedBytes` helper (`@openclaw/media-core/base64`) to estimate decoded byte length before decoding\n- Propagates existing `maxBytes` limit through:\n  - CLI image writing (`writeCliImages`, in `src/agents/cli-runner/cli-images.ts`)\n  - Provider image parsing (`generatedImageAssetFromBase64`)\n  - **Codex/OpenAI OAuth image-generation result route** (`parseOpenAiCompatibleImageResponse` threads `maxBytes`)\n- Boundary tests for configured-limit acceptance, over-limit rejection before decode, default-limit enforcement, and Codex OAuth route oversized-entry drop\n- **No new configuration**: uses the existing `generatedMediaMaxBytes` setting\n- **No new public package API**: the CLI staging guard is a private function in `cli-images.ts` built on the existing `estimateBase64DecodedBytes` export (per review feedback, the earlier `@openclaw/media-core/base64-size-limit` subpath was removed)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real behavior proof (final head, 2026-07-19)\n\nBoth guarded base64 paths were executed directly on the exact PR head via `tsx` (no mocks — real function calls through the public entry `prepareCliPromptImagePayload`, real filesystem staging):\n\n```bash\n./node_modules/.bin/tsx runtime-proof.mts\n```\n\n```text\ndate: Sun Jul 19 2026 08:11:59 GMT+0800 (中国标准时间)\nnode: v24.18.0\ndefault MAX_IMAGE_BYTES=6291456\ncode path: cli-images.ts prepareCliPromptImagePayload + image-assets.ts @ PR head\n[cli staging valid] accepted: imagePaths=1 file=/tmp/openclaw/openclaw-cli-images/6a2b0d3f….png\n[cli staging over-limit] rejected before decode: Base64 payload exceeds size limit: 6295552 bytes > 6291456 bytes\n[provider parser valid] accepted: assets=1 mime=image/png bytes=70\n[provider parser over-limit] rejected before decode: assets=0 (expect 0)\n```\n\n- **CLI staging (`prepareCliPromptImagePayload` → private `writeCliImages` guard)**: a valid 1×1 PNG is staged to a private file; a payload 4 KB over the 6 MiB default budget is rejected by the estimate-before-decode guard with a clear size error — `Buffer.from(data, \"base64\")` is never reached for the over-limit input.\n- **Provider parser (`parseOpenAiCompatibleImageResponse`)**: a valid `b64_json` entry under the budget produces one asset (70 decoded bytes, sniffed `image/png`); the over-limit payload is dropped before decode (`assets=0`).\n\n## Regression tests (final head)\n\n```bash\npnpm vitest run src/agents/cli-runner.helpers.test.ts src/image-generation/image-assets.test.ts \\\n  src/music-generation/provider-assets.test.ts src/agents/cli-runner.spawn.test.ts \\\n  src/agents/cli-runner/claude-live-session.background-tasks.test.ts src/agents/utils/image-resize.test.ts\n```\n\n```text\nTest Files  10 passed (10)\n     Tests  304 passed (304)\n```\n\n(Private helpers are exercised through `cli-images.test-support.ts`, the repo's globalThis test-api pattern; `writeCliSystemPromptFile` is imported from `cli-images.js` directly.)\n\n## What was not tested\n\n- Live provider OOM reproduction (neither necessary nor safely desirable). The proof above exercises the exact guard branches on the final head.\n\n## CI note\n\nEarlier-head failures traced to this branch, not main: a stale `../../sandbox/fs-bridge.js` import path, the moved `writeCliSystemPromptFile` no longer exported from `helpers.ts`, knip unused-export findings (test-only consumers), and unrelated `image-resize.ts` churn. Current head: helpers stay private with test access via `cli-images.test-support.ts`, tests import from `cli-images.js` directly, `image-resize.ts` matches main, and oxlint/knip/tsgo all pass locally. Branch is rebased onto latest main.\n",
        "branch": "fix/base64-decode-before-bounds-unified",
